id: pm-slack-standup-commitment-variance
title: Compare selected standup commitments with revision-cited outcomes and scope changes
description: ""
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-slack-standup#166"
created_at: "2026-10-29T06:33:18.844Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T18:48:07.939Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-29T18:48:07.277Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T18:48:07.277Z"
author: codex-agent
release: 2026.10.29
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T06:33:21.881Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against core command/source search and sibling README contracts: core owns native history, statuses and relationship reads; pm-brief owns acknowledged handoff contracts; pm-slack owns delivery acknowledgments; prior impediment acknowledgments remain separate. This feature compares explicitly selected periodic intent with linked outcome evidence and later scope changes; it assigns no work and sends no reminders. Existing progress deltas supply evidence inspection and verified history. No matching package or core issue was found by commitment variance search."
  "2026-10-29T06:35:09.915Z",codex-agent,"Design: read-only selected source revision with per-comment standup-commitment/v1 declarations. Each declaration binds a key to a native target revision; malformed/foreign annotations are isolated. SDK replay and verified history provide baselines, full intervening scope changes (including ABA), outcome revisions and role-based lifecycle meaning. Report carries no bodies and covers up to twenty keys. No capture/write/import/sync journal is introduced; native comments remain the supported capture mechanism. Re-read source, target and settings witnesses before returning, refusing detected interleaving; a peer can still change state after its final check, and no workspace transaction isolation is claimed (core #1620)."
  "2026-10-29T06:43:49.612Z",codex-agent,"First focused run: 5/8 passed. Three test expectations exposed SDK contracts: canonical body trimming, schema definitions stored separately from settings, and lossless TOON table JSON-column metadata. Adjusted the assertions to use SDK historical reads and decodePmTableRows; custom empty-role statuses now remain unsupported. The twenty-commitment large-body fixture measured 6561 JSON bytes. Added an SDK-backed seeded state model with older-input replays, CRLF variants, all inspected native scope fields, revision binding, random custom role registries and ambient focus."
  "2026-10-29T06:53:21.504Z",codex-agent,"Public-data validation passed against public main 83f4e1ee5d2fde97254c6fa8044f5cc017314691: 107 certified items, 107 reports, 1048 native events, 107 missing captures, 252 foreign comments, zero declared commitments, invalid annotations or refusals, and 220/220 files unchanged (bytes, names, modes and mtimes) with git absent. The twenty explicitly missing-key control returned 20 unsupported rows in 2967 JSON bytes; this is absence evidence, not positive outcome prevalence. Lint/typecheck/docstrings and zero-duplication checks run locally; full release gates remain assigned to CI."
  "2026-10-29T07:00:54.051Z",codex-agent,"Validation passed: focused commitment suite 10/10; both new runtime modules measured 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. The independent SDK state model passed 500 sequences with 3363 native mutations across eight generated custom registries, zero mismatches, older-input/CRLF replays and all inspected native scope fields. Four disposable changed-function reverts (scope detection, target revision binding, missing-capture uncertainty, read-witness validation) each failed an assertion; restored production code passed the three selected regressions. The package worktree was never behaviorally mutated. SDK settings metadata is used to refuse unavailable configuration instead of silently interpreting fallback defaults; legacy format warnings remain readable."
  "2026-10-29T07:01:50.226Z",codex-agent,"Linked native test execution passed 1/1 commands and 10/10 tests. Existing tracker policy disables automatic test-result persistence; no setting was changed. CI will run the unchanged npm and Bun release gates, including the 500-sequence model and all six packed scenarios (npm/Bun current and minimum via npx/bunx plus true npm and Bun global hosts). No import/export/sync writers, native mutation journals or shared package leases are introduced. Remaining concurrency window: a peer may update a previously rechecked stream before other checks finish or after return; observed revisions remain explicit and no atomic snapshot is promised."
  "2026-10-29T07:04:57.113Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/166 . Initial CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/actions/runs/40833074136 . This final tracker handoff will trigger a fresh exact-head run; the PR records its final URL and gate counts. Tracker history integrity passes. Local default health initially refused an inherited global pm-github host-version skew (pinned SDK 2026.10.25 versus extension host 2026.10.28); strict health passes with an isolated global path and extensions disabled, matching clean-checkout isolation. Existing provenance and telemetry advisories remain advisory; no history rewrite, SDK pin bump or telemetry configuration change was made. Item remains unclosed and released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T07:07:51.255Z",codex-agent,"Final documentation check: extracted the published SDK example into a disposable consumer and passed strict TypeScript compilation. The capture example now explicitly checks for the optional host-injected SDK context before invoking native comments; report code and all runtime measurements are unchanged. Clean-checkout CI health and committed build verification passed; final release gates continue on the current PR head."
  "2026-10-29T08:22:27.181Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1 resumed. General violated rule: historical materialization does not establish present target availability; availability must be independently observed and included in the final consistency witness. Audit all report commands, SDK and CLI paths, native JSON/TOON output and packed consumers; retain supported historical reads while refusing or marking unavailable live targets. Re-checking all review findings and adding class-wide adversarial and behavioral-revert evidence. The branch was behind main and main is merged before implementation."
  "2026-10-29T08:25:32.778Z",codex-agent,"Class audit found one shared reader used by commitment variance, historical progress, ordinary standups, decisions and exports: readVerifiedStandupHistory. A missing current document currently skips current-document verification, so retained materialized history can masquerade as available native state. Fix the shared boundary: missing current storage is valid only when SDK replay proves the retained stream ends in a native deleted state. The existing variance recheck then includes availability through the shared reader result/refusal, catching disappearance without a history append. Preserve real SDK deletion history reads. No additional actionable non-blocking findings were present in the supplied round-1 report or GitHub review/comment inventory. Main updated the pinned toolchain; dependencies are installed at main pins before further implementation."
  "2026-10-29T08:35:43.865Z",codex-agent,"The new pre-fix canary failed with actual completed versus expected unsupported after physical target removal with retained history. The fix is at the shared verified-history boundary, not the row classifier. Shared readers now require an existing native document or an SDK-replayed deleted state. Rechecks observe disappearance through that shared result even without a history append. Expanded tests discover all registered commands, exercise SDK and installed JSON/TOON paths and exports, inject source/target removal at every read boundary, and retain native deletion-history compatibility. Packed npm/Bun current/minimum/global consumers now include the same materialization canary. No tests or thresholds were removed or relaxed."
  "2026-10-29T08:43:15.070Z",codex-agent,"Round-1 behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy, reverting only readVerifiedStandupHistory caused both materialization canaries to fail with assertions (2/2): completed versus unsupported and disappearance escaping its recheck. Restoring the fixed reader passed 2/2, with the package worktree implementation untouched. Focused materialization plus unchanged history-readonly suites passed 6/6. Repeated public-main probe at 6e898423bae6c6e71d0f4c474344e53a1dd55693: 107 items/reports, 1048 events, 107 missing captures, 252 foreign annotations, zero invalid annotations/refusals, 220/220 unchanged files; twenty missing-key control remains 2967 JSON bytes. Original functional/model evidence is retained; fresh exact-head CI will run both full npm/Bun release gates with two workers. SDK UX observation: the stale 2026.10.25 claim/update runtime refused after main pinned 2026.10.26, while comment still allowed a write; exact pinned dependencies were reinstalled before all subsequent work. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-29T08:51:46.484Z",codex-agent,"The new linked command passed 1/1 with 3/3 materialization tests; result recording remains disabled by inherited policy. Rebuilt output, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. Refusal remedies now name current native storage as well as retained history. Class audit also covered the legacy certified-list CLI adapter, supplied snapshot/formatter helpers and historical count comparisons: they do not use retained materialization to infer a missing current item; no unrelated historical-input behavior was tightened. Local standalone packed acceptance is continuing through its six consumers, and fresh exact-head CI will provide full npm/Bun gate evidence at unchanged limits. All review findings supplied in this round are addressed by the shared guard and cross-path regressions."
  "2026-10-29T09:25:12.408Z",codex-agent,"Reached the required 30-minute CI wait cutoff for runtime fix head 1d7355bf848b21a5fa78aa539c7043208d7d4be7. Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/actions/runs/40845372345 : Node 26 npm and Bun full release gates each passed 315/315 tests, zero failures/skips, all four coverage dimensions at 100 across 18 sources, and 6/6 packed materialization scenarios. Windows passed 6/6 packed scenarios. Local standalone packed acceptance also passed all 6 with materialization_verified true at pinned 2026.10.26 and minimum 2026.10.20. Node 22.18 full gates remain in progress after queue delay; this is missing evidence, not approval. Recording this tracker-only handoff creates a new head that needs fresh exact-head CI; runtime files are unchanged. Preserve the pending run for the orchestrator pipeline. Claim remains released and the item unclosed."
